  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The length of the tangent drawn from any point on the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}+2 f y+\\lambda=0$ to the circle $\\mathrm{x}^{2}+\\mathrm{y}^{2}+2 \\mathrm{fy}+\\mu=0,$ where $\\mu>\\lambda>0,$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XY0BX",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\mu-\\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7t9k9",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\mu+\\lambda}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mYEH3",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\mu^{2}-\\lambda^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3CIwX",
      "text": "$\\mu+\\lambda$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the radius of the first circle be $\\mathrm{CT}=\\mathrm{r}_{1}$. Also, let the radius of the second circle be $\\mathrm{CP}=\\mathrm{r}_{2}$\r\nIn the triangle $\\mathrm{PCT}, \\mathrm{T}$ is a right angle\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/Vx6mkKDSQTkMXkiFF9Z4ygG5UGK_UM5zCD04GOUxX60.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text { So, } P T &=\\sqrt{P C^{2}-C T^{2}}=\\sqrt{r_{1}^{2}-r_{2}^{2}} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\left(f^{2}-\\lambda\\right)-\\left(f^{2}-\\mu\\right)}=\\sqrt{\\mu-\\lambda} \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
